// Title: HackTool - EDRSilencer Execution
// Sigma ID: eb2d07d4-49cb-4523-801a-da002df36602
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: @gott_cyber
// Date: 2024-01-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects the execution of EDRSilencer, a tool that leverages Windows Filtering Platform (WFP) to
//   block Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR) agents from reporting security events to the server
//   based on PE metadata information.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/netero1010/EDRSilencer
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_edrsilencer.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\EDRSilencer.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "EDRSilencer.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription contains "EDRSilencer"
